Chapter: FactSyncTruncatedTest
  cites Trust chapter FactSync
  cites Trust chapter AgentProtocol
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Net chapter MessageFraming
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A sync bundle arrives from a peer, so the element count and every field length
 are the peer's to choose. Three things are under test.

 THE ABSORB REFUSAL. A truncated reply must leave the store untouched rather
 than merge the facts that arrived before the cut. The store is what the trust
 lattice reasons over, so a half-read fact in it is worse than no sync.

 THE OFFER REFUSAL, which is a disclosure control and not only a correctness
 one. `fact-sync-answer-offer` replies with every fact the offer did not list.
 A truncated offer decoded to a SHORT hash list, and a short list means fewer
 facts excluded, so a peer that cut its own offer short harvested the whole
 store. The arm below cuts an offer naming both of the responder's facts and
 asserts the reply carries none of them.

 THE COUNT ARM is the heap half. Both list decoders were driven by a leading
 le32 with no relation to the buffer; the payload below declares 4294967295
 elements over four bytes. The same shape ablated in `crf-decode-events` died
 `OUT OF MEMORY` in 6 seconds rather than answering, so this arm kills the run
 when it regresses instead of printing a wrong line.

 THE LEAK ROW is the measurement that pays, and it needs its control read
 beside it. Every prefix of the offer must draw ZERO facts, but so does a whole
 offer that legitimately names both, so all-zeros alone proves nothing. The
 control is `empty-offer reply-facts=2`, which shows disclosure is reachable at
 all. Measured with the refusal removed from `fact-sync-answer-offer`, the row
 read `22222222221111110`: a peer that cut its own offer short was handed the
 responder's entire store.

Section: Helpers

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "v" else "x"

  mk : Text -> Fact
  mk (h) = Fact { hash = h, kind = DefinitionFact, content = h, author = "", timestamp = 0 }

  cut : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  cut (xs) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else cut xs n (i + 1) (acc & [list-at xs i])

  me : AgentIdentity = AgentIdentity { public-key = [1] }

  them : AgentIdentity = AgentIdentity { public-key = [2] }

Section: Test Data

 The responder holds h1 and h2. The offer names both, so a whole offer draws a
 reply of nothing and only a MISREAD offer draws facts out of the store.

  holder : BareFactStore = fact-store (fact-store fact-store-empty (mk "h1")) (mk "h2")

  whole-offer : SyncOfferMsg = fact-sync-make-offer holder me

  huge-count : List Integer = [255, 255, 255, 255]

  reply-of : List Integer -> SyncReplyMsg
  reply-of (payload) = SyncReplyMsg { from = them, payload = payload }

  offer-of : List Integer -> SyncOfferMsg
  offer-of (payload) = SyncOfferMsg { from = them, payload = payload }

 Both sweeps run over every prefix. `offer` records whether the decode was
 believed and `leak` records how many facts the reply handed back at that depth,
 which is the number that must stay at zero until the offer is whole.

  sweep-offer : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  sweep-offer (whole) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else sweep-offer whole n (i + 1) (acc & yn ((sync-decode-hashes (cut whole i 0 [])).valid))

  sweep-leak : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  sweep-leak (whole) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else let r = fact-sync-answer-offer holder me (offer-of (cut whole i 0 []))
    in let got = list-length ((sync-decode-facts (r.payload)).facts)
    in sweep-leak whole n (i + 1) (acc & show got)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let op = whole-offer.payload
    in let reply = fact-sync-answer-offer holder me whole-offer
    in let full-reply = fact-sync-answer-offer holder me (offer-of (sync-encode-hashes []))
    in let cut-absorb = fact-sync-absorb-reply fact-store-empty (reply-of (cut (full-reply.payload) 12 0 []))
    in let whole-absorb = fact-sync-absorb-reply fact-store-empty full-reply
    in let huge-absorb = fact-sync-absorb-reply fact-store-empty (reply-of huge-count)
    in act
      print-line-uni ("offer len=" & show (list-length op) & " valid=" & yn ((sync-decode-hashes op).valid) & " hashes=" & show (list-length ((sync-decode-hashes op).hashes)))
      print-line-uni ("whole-offer reply-facts=" & show (list-length ((sync-decode-facts (reply.payload)).facts)))
      print-line-uni ("empty-offer reply-facts=" & show (list-length ((sync-decode-facts (full-reply.payload)).facts)))
      print-line-uni ("whole-absorb count=" & show (fact-count whole-absorb) & " h1=" & yn (fact-has whole-absorb "h1"))
      print-line-uni ("cut-absorb count=" & show (fact-count cut-absorb) & " h1=" & yn (fact-has cut-absorb "h1"))
      print-line-uni ("huge-count valid=" & yn ((sync-decode-facts huge-count).valid) & " absorb=" & show (fact-count huge-absorb))
      print-line-uni ("huge-hashes valid=" & yn ((sync-decode-hashes huge-count).valid))
      print-line-uni ("offer-valid 0.." & show (list-length op) & " = " & sweep-offer op (list-length op) 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("leak 0.." & show (list-length op) & " = " & sweep-leak op (list-length op) 0 "")
    end
  end
